          "session_id": "5096da06-04f7-4b7d-894b-30084fc499fc",
          "position": 8,
          "content": "Что делает пример с рекламой, если timed Future.get не успел вернуть результат?",
          "answer": "Если timed Future.get не успел вернуть результат, задача по загрузке рекламы отменяется. [DOC:structure-0057]\nВместо недоступной рекламы используется реклама по умолчанию. [DOC:structure-0056] [DOC:structure-0057]",
          "status": "done",
          "kind": "question",
          "question_scope": "document",
          "search_question": "What does the advertisement example do if timed Future.get did not return a result?",
          "sources": [
            {
              "kind": "document",
              "chunk_id": "structure-0057",
              "source": "https://jcip.net/jcip-sample.pdf",
              "title": "Java Concurrency in Practice — sample chapter",
              "section": "6.3.7 Placing time limits on tasks",
              "page_start": 19,
              "page_end": 19
            },
            {
              "kind": "document",
              "chunk_id": "structure-0056",
              "source": "https://jcip.net/jcip-sample.pdf",
              "title": "Java Concurrency in Practice — sample chapter",
              "section": "6.3.7 Placing time limits on tasks",
              "page_start": 19,
              "page_end": 19
            }
          ],
          "citations": [
            {
              "chunk_id": "structure-0057",
              "quote": "It submits the ad-fetching task to an executor, com- putes the rest of the page content, and then waits for the ad until its time budget runs out.8 If the get times out, it cancels9 the ad-fetching task and uses a default advertisement instead."
            },
            {
              "chunk_id": "structure-0056",
              "quote": "For example, a web application may fetch its advertisements from an external ad server, but if the ad is not available within two seconds, it instead displays a default advertisement so that ad unavailability does not under mine the site’s responsiveness requirements."
            }
          ],
          "grounding_status": "answered",
          "error": null,
